# AWS S3 Data Migration & Synchronization

An automated AWS S3 bucket provisioning and data sync project completed as part of the Nautilus DevOps tasks on KodeKloud.

## 📌 Project Overview

The objective of this project was to perform a secure, zero-data-loss migration from an existing Amazon S3 bucket (`datacenter-s3-384482213`) to a newly provisioned private S3 bucket (`datacenter-sync-384482213`) in the `us-east-1` region using the AWS CLI.

## 🛠️ Infrastructure & Tools

* **Cloud Provider:** Amazon Web Services (AWS)
* **Storage Service:** Amazon Simple Storage Service (S3)
* **Command-Line Tool:** AWS CLI (`aws s3api`, `aws s3`)
* **Region:** `us-east-1`

## 🚀 Implementation Steps

### 1. Provision New Private S3 Bucket
Created a dedicated, private S3 destination bucket in the `us-east-1` region:

```bash
aws s3api create-bucket --bucket datacenter-sync-384482213 --region us-east-1

2. Verify Bucket Availability
Confirmed active creation and permissions using the head-bucket API call:

aws s3api head-bucket --bucket datacenter-sync-384482213

3. Data Migration & Sync
Synchronized all objects, directory structures, and metadata from the source bucket to the destination bucket:

aws s3 sync s3://datacenter-s3-384482213 s3://datacenter-sync-384482213

4. Data Consistency Verification
Extracted detailed recursive lists with summaries for both buckets and compared output using diff to guarantee zero missing files or corrupted byte counts:

# Summarize source bucket contents
aws s3 ls s3://datacenter-s3-384482213 --recursive --summarize > /tmp/source.txt

# Summarize destination bucket contents
aws s3 ls s3://datacenter-sync-384482213 --recursive --summarize > /tmp/dest.txt

# Validate identical object count and file sizes
diff /tmp/source.txt /tmp/dest.txt

✅ Results & Validation
Total Objects Transferred: 3,782 objects

Total Volume Migrated: ~110.07 MB (110,075,734 bytes)

Integrity Status: PASSED (Zero diff discrepancies between source and target buckets)

